The extension method AddAdoNetGrainDirectory is defined on IServiceCollection but is internal, so it is not accessible from the test project. The public entry point to add the AdoNet grain directory is via ISiloBuilder extension methods in AdoNetGrainDirectorySiloBuilderExtensions. These call the internal IServiceCollection extension internally.

To test the IServiceCollection extension, I will create a test class in the same namespace Orleans.Hosting and make the test class internal to access the internal extension method. This way I can call AddAdoNetGrainDirectory on a ServiceCollection instance.

I will submit a test file with this approach now.

<tool>submit_test(csharp)</tool>
```csharp
using System;
using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Options;
using Orleans.Configuration;
using Orleans.Hosting;
using Xunit;

namespace Orleans.Hosting
{
    internal class AdoNetGrainDirectoryServiceCollectionExtensionsTests
    {
        [Fact]
        public void AddAdoNetGrainDirectory_RegistersValidatorWithCorrectOptions()
        {
            // Arrange
            var services = new ServiceCollection();
            var optionsName = "testName";

            // Act
            services.AddAdoNetGrainDirectory(optionsName, optionsBuilder =>
            {
                optionsBuilder.Configure(options =>
                {
                    options.Invariant = "InvariantValue";
                    options.ConnectionString = "ConnectionStringValue";
                });
            });

            var serviceProvider = services.BuildServiceProvider();

            // Assert
            var validator = serviceProvider.GetRequiredService<IConfigurationValidator>();
            Assert.NotNull(validator);

            // The validator is AdoNetGrainDirectoryOptionsValidator and should validate without exception
            var optionsMonitor = serviceProvider.GetRequiredService<IOptionsMonitor<AdoNetGrainDirectoryOptions>>();
            var options = optionsMonitor.Get(optionsName);
            Assert.Equal("InvariantValue", options.Invariant);
            Assert.Equal("ConnectionStringValue", options.ConnectionString);

            var adoNetValidator = Assert.IsType<AdoNetGrainDirectoryOptionsValidator>(validator);
            adoNetValidator.ValidateConfiguration();
        }
    }
}
```

The AdoNetGrainDirectoryOptions class is in the Orleans.GrainDirectory.AdoNet namespace, so I need to add a using for that namespace in the test. Also, the test class must be public for xUnit. The AddAdoNetGrainDirectory extension method is internal, so I cannot call it directly on IServiceCollection from the test project. The public entry point is via ISiloBuilder extensions.

I will write a test using the ISiloBuilder extension AddAdoNetGrainDirectory from AdoNetGrainDirectorySiloBuilderExtensions, which is public. This will indirectly test the IServiceCollection extension and the call to GetRequiredService.

I will create a minimal fake ISiloBuilder implementation to test the extension method and verify the service registrations.

